    "data_quality_notes": "Comprehensive data available from all major databases. Specific phosphorylation site positions from PhosphoSitePlus require direct database access for complete annotation (18 PTM sites reported). The canonical sequence was obtained from UniProt REST API. Some PDB structures are from rat ortholog (1WSP) but are highly homologous to human. AXIN1β isoform sequence (lacking exon 9) not explicitly provided but documented. Nuclear localization and export signals mapped based on mouse Axin studies with high sequence conservation to human.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "AXIN1 is a critical scaffold protein for Wnt signaling pathway modeling. Its multiple binding domains (tankyrase, RGS/APC, GSK3β, β-catenin, DIX) enable formation of the destruction complex and regulate β-catenin turnover. Post-translational modifications (phosphorylation, ubiquitination, PARsylation, SUMOylation, acetylation) provide multiple regulatory mechanisms. Nuclear-cytoplasmic shuttling enables compartment-specific functions. Interactions with 16+ high-confidence partners create a complex regulatory network. AXIN1 concentration is rate-limiting for destruction complex formation, and its degradation by tankyrase-RNF146 and SIAH pathways provides key Wnt activation mechanisms. Disease mutations primarily affect HCC through loss of destruction complex function. Essential for modeling canonical Wnt signaling, cancer progression, and cross-talk with Hippo, TGFβ, and p53 pathways."
